; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Hilbert Curve
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, space filling curve, parity, color
; SUMMARY:  Draws a Hilbert curve that visits every cell of a 64 by 64 grid without crossing itself.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The Hilbert curve is one unbroken line that snakes through a
;   square, visiting every small cell exactly once and never
;   crossing itself. Each level is made of four copies of the level
;   below, two of them turned on their side. The color changes as
;   the line goes, so you can see the four quarters.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the level on the last line (1 to 7). The step
;   size is worked out for you so the curve always fills the same
;   square.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a :parity input of 1 or -1 that mirrors the drawing
;   * MINUS to flip the parity for the side copies
;   * POWER to compute the grid size from the level
;   * coloring by how far along the path you are
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw levels 1, 2 and 3 to see the U shape being reused.
;   * Use a thick pen and a small level for a maze-like look.
;   * Start with parity 1 at the bottom right corner instead.
; ============================================================

; HILBERT draws one Hilbert curve. Between the four smaller curves
; the turtle takes three single steps that join them up.
to hilbert :level :parity
  if :level = 0 [stop]
  left 90 * :parity
  hilbert :level - 1 minus :parity
  join.step
  right 90 * :parity
  hilbert :level - 1 :parity
  join.step
  hilbert :level - 1 :parity
  right 90 * :parity
  join.step
  hilbert :level - 1 minus :parity
  left 90 * :parity
end

; JOIN.STEP takes one step and picks the next color of the rainbow.
to join.step
  make "steps :steps + 1
  localmake "t :steps / :total
  setpencolor (list 255 * :t 120 + 100 * sin (180 * :t) 255 * (1 - :t))
  forward :size
end

; DRAW.HILBERT works out the step so the curve fills a 500 square.
to draw.hilbert :level
  ; At level n the curve has 2^n cells along a side and 4^n - 1 steps.
  make "size 500 / ((power 2 :level) - 1)
  make "total (power 4 :level) - 1
  make "steps 0
  penup setxy -250 -250 setheading 0 pendown
  ; Parity -1 makes the first turn a right turn, so the curve heads
  ; into the square instead of off the left edge.
  hilbert :level -1
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 30]
setpensize 3
draw.hilbert 6
